# Prettier writes LF and every step in `npm run check` reads the working tree, so the
# working tree is kept on LF as well. Without this, a Windows clone with
# core.autocrlf=true converts files to CRLF on checkout, which makes Git warn on every
# `git add` and leaves the checkout disagreeing with the formatter. This repository is
# developed on Windows with autocrlf=true, so the line matters here rather than being
# boilerplate.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Assets, which must never be line-ending normalized. png, jpg, ico and wav are the
# formats actually in the repository; jpeg, gif, webp and svg are listed because an
# image added later would otherwise be corrupted silently by the rule above, and finding
# that out afterwards is worse than four unused lines.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.webp binary
*.svg  binary
*.ico  binary
*.wav  binary

# Machine-written and not worth reading as a diff. It is the only generated file that is
# committed: js/game.js and dist/ are both generated too, but both are in .gitignore and
# rebuilt by `npm run build`, so they need no attributes at all.
package-lock.json -diff linguist-generated
